    {
      "id": "d7737fx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Characteristics of Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plants are eukaryotic, multicellular organisms characterized by cell walls made of cellulose and autotrophic nutrition.",
        "Plant cells contain specialized structures including chloroplasts, rigid cell walls, and large central vacuoles.",
        "Plant tissues are categorized into Meristematic (dividing) and Permanent tissues (complex transport tissues like Xylem and Phloem).",
        "Photosynthesis converts solar energy, carbon dioxide, and water into oxygen and chemical energy (glucose).",
        "Plant growth and responses are regulated by key hormones including Auxins, Gibberellins, Cytokinins, Ethylene, and Abscisic Acid."
      ],
      "id": "goh8nni"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pjatljg",
      "content": "• Plants are multicellular eukaryotic organisms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zq3ixyh",
      "content": "• They contain chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hojui9m",
      "content": "• Cell walls are made of cellulose."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w3dhq3n",
      "content": "• They are generally non‑motile."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y4jrw0a",
      "content": "• They store food mainly in the form of starch."
    },
    {
