    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently distinguish Xylem (water conduction, unidirectional, mostly dead cells) from Phloem (food conduction, bidirectional, mostly living cells).",
        "Focus on Plant Hormones: Auxin causes apical dominance, Cytokinin promotes cell division, Ethylene induces fruit ripening, and Abscisic Acid causes stomatal closure.",
        "Vegetative propagation methods (tubers, rhizomes, runners) are commonly tested under asexual plant reproduction."
      ],
      "id": "f3agxij"
